{
  "name": "@dustinedwards/site-runtime",
  "version": "0.141.1",
  "private": true,
  "description": "The portfolio sites' shared runtime. Today: OWASP Secure Headers Project defaults, a Content-Security-Policy built from a per-site list of what a site loads, the post players a page may embed (frame-src and their Permissions-Policy features), the site registry the builder and the check share, the check a site runs in CI to prove its responses carry them and the live check against a deployed site, one exact rate limiter on a SQLite Durable Object, the members model: layers, permission bundles and end dates for an app with staff, the Access for SaaS sign-in, the MCP servers' consent page, sign-in handler, owner page (grants with Revoke, agent keys, the tool-call log), tool-call log (with its export, retention and alert), server scaffold (tool registration by grant, abort plumbing, outside-text results, the tool list's rules and pin), the admin MCP Worker built from them (door, provider, sign-in, health and the log's cron), named agent keys and the list-only test key, the Cloudflare Access request-token check and admin check, the check that an Access application's policies match the site's admins, one HTML escape, one constant-time secret compare, the one mail send over the send_email binding, the /health response with its checks, the security.txt file, responsive images resized by the Images binding (a GIF kept animated, with its still first frame for reduced motion), their props for JSX, the edits a site writes back (turn, mirror, shrink, a change of format) and the live check of a site's images and media, link prefetch through speculation rules, preloads declared once for the page and the Early Hints header, public pages stored at the edge and purged by tag, the share-card image and its route (edge cache, cross-origin, 503 on failure), one set of byte encodings (hex, base64, base64url, SHA-256), the signed token behind emailed links (with key rotation), where a site's Anthropic calls go (AI Gateway or direct), the one Anthropic Messages caller (timeout, one retry layer, stop reasons, structured output, prompt caching, one model registry checked against the deprecations page), starting a Claude Code routine, the check on AI-written prose with the measure of an author's voice, the one sign-in every site offers (passkey, email link and code, Google and Apple, and a code-only request for a phone app) with the sign-in page's server side (its form action, words, landing check, social start, account options, the account page's posts and the disposable-address refusal), its auth event log and security history, fresh sign-in checks, security notices, sessions list, passkey names and WebAuthn signals, the Cloudflare Turnstile widget loader and its fail-closed server check, the operator API door a site serves Capsid through (bearer, rate limit, named tools), the same-origin check for resource routes, who may see a draft, the trailing-slash redirect, the gone (410) list and the slug-rename redirect, the static _headers file and the one bin that writes it from the registry, one structured log line with its scrubbers and request fields, the 404 counter with its referrers and report, scheduled jobs with their record, the signed-in crawl an app runs on its own pages for the scoreboard, the one React Router server entry with its nonce context, the one Worker (gateway, Renderer, request log and cron), the small request helpers (caller address, plain never-cached answers, the timed fetch, the Worker Preview flag, the public origin), D1's statement limits (IN lists and inserts cut to fit, LIKE patterns escaped), CSV exports guarded against formulas, and the co-editing room a file's editors share (the Durable Object behind Capsomer's collab editor), a job under a fenced lease and the alarm ticker for sub-hourly jobs, a secret sealed at rest under a rotating keyring, Web Push from the Worker, HTML to PDF with Browser Rendering, /health's verdict kept for a page tile with one mail when a check changes, RFC 9457 problem details for every JSON API's errors, the preview-then-perform confirmation token, the Hono doors a site's API shares (operator bearer, rate limit), a cron history with its states and a daily mail about a job that is not well (or any alert raised at most once a day), the AI budget (an exact daily count on a Durable Object, a soft cap in KV, reserve then settle), an ask box's stream frames, answer key and answer guard, a share card's layout with its title sizes and key, and the newsletter's double opt-in.",
